			<div class="content" id="post-content-1899770">
									

<p>Thanks for the feedback! Short answer: You didn't miss anything. I simply neglected to explain any pseudo-science behind this, which was an error on my part.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Long&nbsp;Answer</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Hide</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>I am well-aware of Relativity and the size of our galaxy. I am also aware of at least one theory that certain Neutrinos might actually be faster-than-light <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tachyon#Neutrinos">Tachyons</a>. Since the Foundation isn't able to differentiate different Neutrinos from each other (humans can barely detect Neutrinos as it is, much less categorize them), they didn't realize that the beam was actually an instantaneous, Relativity-breaking communications beam. They just thought it was a normal transmission. By breaking the beam (the &quot;Tripwire&quot;) they inadvertently set off some anomalous alien retro-causal Doomsday Device without realizing it. Think about the &quot;Dead Hand&quot; Nuclear deterrent that the Soviets use, or the similar dead-man-switch Nuclear Weapons systems the USA uses. This is that on a galactic scale. The Foundation is a colony of ants chewing at the wires of the Dead Hand switch and they set it off and it retroactively wiped out an alien civilization.</p>
<p>In order to keep causality alive and time flowing in the same direction, the retroactive <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Light_cone">Light Cones</a> reach the detonator (the complex) at the exact moment AFTER the switch is triggered.</p>
