			<div class="content" id="post-content-1900223">
									

<p>I wonder, are addendums legitimately used in the special containment procedures? Not saying it's good or bad, but I think I never seen one there. Chronologically, the addendum would fit better at the end.</p>
<p>You know what also caught my eye? The recurring 2&#160;7&#160;1. Could you, at least in a collapsible, say what did you have in mind?</p>
<p>As with the sycamore seed shaped aliens&#8230; interesting. Just that, interesting. No more, no less. They possibly have deactivated the consoles so humans don't tinker with it further&#8230;</p>
<p>The Event Omega surely sparks some interest, too, and I think I know what is my main issue with this SCP being in the 2000 slot.</p>
<p>It's audience is too specific. Me, and I bet many others just don't know what's going on here, much less able to draw any conclusions of what could have happened as a result of Event Omega or about anything else that happened in the SCP. I don't even know what a neutrino is. And the Foundation documents should be understandable to most people that read them; many complex ones do this justice. Iapetus, Bigfoot, 233, several 001 proposals come to mind. I feel that if I knew what was going on, being more knowledgable with astrophysics / chemistry, I could properly upvote/downvote, but as is, I have to give a tentative no vote as your regular scp-wiki reader Joe.</p>

