			<div class="content" id="post-content-1900344">
									

<p>Hey, thanks for the feedback, and the interest. I appreciate that more than anything else!</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Long&nbsp;Answer</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Hide</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Good eye with the 271 thing. So 2.71828&#8230; is an approximation for the mathematical constant <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/E_(mathematical_constant)">e</a>. It's an irrational number, like pi, that shows up all over math/nature/physics. It's found in population growth algorithms, computing interest accrual, and practically everywhere in calculus. It's an important number to our universe.</p>
<p>One thing you may have never thought about is that humans use a base 10 numbering system (0s 1s 2s 3s&#8230; 9s). Computers use base 2. (1s and 0s), but you can also have base 3 (0s, 1s, 2s) or any other base. The Mayans used base 20, the Babylonians used base 60. Really, the best guess for why everyone uses base 10 these days is because humans have ten fingers and ten toes. Well you can ALSO use fractional bases. You could use base 1.5. Or base 5.6. Or base pi. The aliens happen use base e. So notice how 10 and multiples of 10 show up everywhere in our stuff. Something is always 10 meters wide or 20 meters tall or takes 100 seconds to complete or 1000 miles from here to there or 850 whatever&#8230; all multiples of 10. The aliens don't use multiples of 10. They use e, and so their structures naturally show multiples of e for the same reason ours show multiples of 10. This isn't important to the overall theme of the skip, its just a little something I threw in because I find it interesting and I was hoping people might ask about it and/or be intrigued.</p>
<p>You are right about the Sycamore aliens. They are alien maintenance men who noticed some weird signal coming from the Earth site and showed up to check things out. They just found a bunch of meddling earthlings messing things up they do the prudent thing&#8230; stun the Earthlings and remove all the obsolete equipment just to make sure the Earthlings can't meddle. It's like a maintenance guy showing up at a Nuclear silo and seeing a bunch of ants eating the wires of a now-obsolete system so they safely remove the wires knowing that the ants can't really hurt anything else. Except that they're wrong, because these ants have dangerous SCPs at their disposal and actually do end up setting off the nuke.</p>
<p>You are probably right about the specific audience. I just don't know what to do about that. It's a sciency SCP, cuz science is my thing. You are right that this wouldn't make a good SCP-2000&#8230; even I know that there are much better candidates out there. I was simply hoping to stay in the positives so that I might get a good 2000 slot. Maybe SCP-2718&#8230;</p>
<p>Thanks again for the interest!</p>
</div>
